# Hello via synchronous Flow.invoke()

```kotlin
fun main() {
    flow {
        emit("Hello")
    }.invoke()
}

suspend fun <T> Flow<T>.invoke(action: suspend (T) -> Unit = {}) {
    collect(action)
}
```

Or more directly:

```kotlin
fun main() {
    flow {
        emit("Hello")
    }.collect { println(it) }
}
```

Note: `Flow.collect()` is inherently **suspend**, so you need a coroutine context:

```kotlin
fun main() = runBlocking {
    flow { emit("Hello") }.collect { println(it) }
}
```

